cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata from this file."
title: "RAPTOR: Containerized Photogrammetry Pipeline for DJI UAVs"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Gómez Cardona"
    given-names: "Federico"
    email: "fjgomezc@eafit.edu.co"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-8525-4354"
    affiliation: "SIATA, Sistema de Alerta Temprana de Medellín y el Valle de Aburrá; Universidad EAFIT"
version: "1.0.0"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/federicogmz/raptor"
url: "https://github.com/federicogmz/raptor"
abstract: >-
  Open-source containerized photogrammetry pipeline for DJI UAVs (M3T, H20T, M3M).
  Processes RGB, radiometric thermal, and multispectral imagery to generate orthomosaics,
  surface models, thermal maps, and vegetation indices (NDVI, NDRE, MSAVI2) with an
  interactive Leaflet web geovisor.
keywords:
  - "photogrammetry"
  - "UAV"
  - "drones"
  - "DJI"
  - "thermal imaging"
  - "multispectral"
  - "NDVI"
  - "remote sensing"
  - "geospatial"
